# Rewrite rules for go.referwith50.com, kept here as the written record.
# NOTE: Render does NOT read this file. The live rules are set by hand in the
# Render dashboard (fifty-platform-pages -> Redirects/Rewrites), so a change here
# does nothing until the same rule is added there. Current dashboard rules:
# /r/* , /login and /reps. Format (Netlify-style) used below:
#   <source>  <destination>  <status>
# Status 200 = rewrite (mask): the browser URL bar stays at <source>,
# but the response body is <destination>'s content. Anything else
# (301, 302, ...) is a visible redirect that changes the URL bar.
#
# /login -> fifty-template-dealer.html: a short, memorable URL for the
# staff/admin sign-in page, instead of making people type or link to the
# raw .html filename. Kept as a 200 rewrite (not a redirect) so
# go.referwith50.com/login is the URL people actually see and bookmark.
/login  /fifty-template-dealer.html  200

# Share links (/r/<code>) are served by the API so link-preview crawlers
# (Facebook, iMessage, ...) get tenant-specific Open Graph tags; visitors
# are redirected on to the lead page. See api/src/routes/sharePreview.js.
/r/*  https://five0-platform.onrender.com/r/:splat  200

# /settings: the page behind the gear at the foot of the dealer dashboard.
# Linked from inside the app by its .html name, so it works without this rule
# -- this is the short URL to add in the dashboard when somebody needs to be
# sent straight to it. (There is no /playbook rule: the playbook is 50.'s own
# PDF in the Supabase brand-uploads bucket, not a page in this repo.)
/settings  /fifty-settings.html  200

# manifest.webmanifest is served from the repo root as itself -- no rule
# needed, noted here only because start_url is "/login", which does need the
# rewrite above it to exist.

# /reps -> fifty-reps.html: the sales-rep admin page (50. staff only; the API enforces it).
/reps  /fifty-reps.html  200
